Solution Using test_and_set()
 Mutual-exclusion implementation with test_and_set().
 Shared boolean variable lock, initialized to false.
 Solution:
do {
while (test_and_set(&lock)) 
; /* do nothing */ 
/* critical section */ 
lock = false; 
/* remainder section */ 
} while (true);
 The important characteristic of this instruction is that it is executed
atomically.
• If the machine supports the test_and_set() instruction, then we can implement
mutual exclusion by declaring a boolean variable lock, initialized to false.
 Does it solve the critical-section problem (satisfy the three requirements)? NO. A
process can wait indefinitely for another process that is accessing its CS. There is no
queue maintained, so any new process that finds the lock to be false again can enter.
mutual exclusion and progress are ensured but bounded waiting is not ensured.
