Solution using compare_and_swap
 Shared integer  lock initialized to 0.
 Mutual exclusion using CAS can be provided as follows:
• A global variable (lock) is declared and is initialized to 0.
• The first process that invokes compare_and_swap() will set lock to 1. It will
then enter its critical section.
 Solution: Mutual exclusion with the compare_and_swap() instruction.
while (true){
while (compare_and_swap(&lock, 0, 1) != 0) 
; /* do nothing */ 
/* critical section */ 
lock = 0; 
/* remainder section */ 
} 
 Does it solve the critical-section problem (satisfy the three requirements)? NO
• Although this algorithm satisfies the mutual-exclusion and progress
requirements, it does not satisfy the bounded-waiting requirement.
