Semaphore
 Synchronization tool that provides more sophisticated ways (than Mutex
locks) for processes to synchronize their activities.
 Semaphore S – integer variable.
 S can only be accessed via two indivisible (atomic) operations.
• wait() andsignal()
 Originally calledP() andV()
 Definition of thewait() operation:
wait(S) {
while (S <= 0)
; // busy wait
S--;
}
 Definition of thesignal() operation:
signal(S) {
S++;
}

